-- §SITE_TASK_PATCH (bim-compiler prompts/MOBILE_PERF.md WO-25 "The desktop processor"): the Request Type "Site Task" and its Status Category, as ordinary rows (no dictionary or schema change).
-- ONE source: build_ad_seed_patch.sh copies this file into ad_seed.db.sql, and viewer/mission_processor.js applies the same file to a store that already has its patch applied (OPFS).
-- The SAME rows, with the SAME UUs, exist on the legacy pilot: bim-compiler scripts/bridge/pilot/site_task_status.sql. Ids sit in the high band the seed keeps for its own rows (990000+).
-- Statuses in SeqNo order: New (default, open) -> Prepared (open) -> On site (open) -> Reported (open) -> Verified (closed, final close).
-- Next_Status_ID follows that order. LEGACY NOTE (MStatus.java:268-282 beforeSave; RequestProcessor.java:431-437): legacy keeps Next_Status_ID only for a timeout (TimeoutDays > 0) and clears it on a save otherwise;
--   the Request Processor moves a request on only when TimeoutDays > 0. These rows set no timeout, so nothing moves by itself; the processor reads the order from SeqNo when Next_Status_ID is cleared.
